# Normalize line endings on commit and check out LF everywhere.
#
# `text=auto` alone still checks out CRLF on Windows (core.autocrlf), and `oxfmt --check`
# compares the working copy: a fresh clone then reports every file as unformatted, and a
# `git checkout --` of one file re-introduces the false positive. Pinning `eol=lf` makes the
# checked-out bytes match what the formatter wrote, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Husky hooks are executed by sh: CRLF there breaks the hook.
.husky/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
